From e060d5396288d8297bcd4f2ada5744b691298eca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ruscher <rruscher@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 08:21:18 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 174/178] Clip: Icons on a grid, as Window Maker's: Beside each
 other, with holes.

Window Maker's Clip places its icons on a grid around it (wDockSnapIcon,
case WM_CLIP): Any free cell on the output next to another icon (also
diagonally) takes an icon. The Clip here was a column in one order: A
dock-app dropped beside another (or beside the Clip) was not attached,
and its drop removed it (terminated, put in Removed).

* clip_grid: The cells, Window Maker's snapping, bounds on the output,
  and giving cells to icons of a state from before (the column's order)
  or off a smaller output (shown elsewhere, stored cell kept).
* clip: Lane 0 is the Clip's dock (holes are empty tiles); each other
  lane with dock-apps is a dock of its own at that distance from the
  edge, without an exclusive zone. Publishes Cells/Origin for wlmdock.
* dockapps: Host for tiles spread over docks; cells stored by name in
  Dockapps.plist (Cells = { Order = { name = "lane,slot"; }; }).
* dock_launchers: A launcher's cell is its `Cell` key in State.plist.
* tile_drag: Snapping on the grid; a taken cell refuses the drop (it
  goes back, never removed); icons keep their cells (stored before any
  move: nothing shifts); back on its own cell an icon always stays.
* layer_panel: The Clip's launchers by cell; elsewhere the pointer goes
  through.
* wlmdock: The Clip's launchers in their cells (tilebox grid mode).
* toolkit box: No margin drawn between two placeholders (empty tiles).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
